<key_info>Bug: RELEASE crashes when libstdc++ _Fac_tidy_reg_t destructor accesses _Fac_node objects that were allocated in custom heap's 10MB buffer (now freed)

Failed approaches:
1. Global constructor iostream init - facets allocated later during main()
2. Heap exhaustion - would cause abort() on subsequent allocs
3. Aggressive early init - same as #1

Root cause: _Fac_node and their _Facptr data use custom heap in RELEASE (::operator new), but malloc in DEBUG. Static destructor runs AFTER custom heap freed.

New strategy: Use std::quick_exit() in user_cleanup() to exit process before static destructors run, preventing crash while allowing OS cleanup</key_info>
